# Aesthetica ML Training Pipeline - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is the **Aesthetica ML Training Pipeline** - a comprehensive machine learning workflow for image classification using CLIP embeddings and Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) models. The pipeline processes raw image datasets through embedding generation to trained model deployment.

## Project Structure
```
aesthetica/
├── src/                          # Main source code
│   ├── train_model_mlp.py       # Core MLP training script with SimpleDashboard
│   ├── data_to_csv.py           # Raw image dataset → CSV conversion
│   ├── dataset_to_embeddings.py # CSV → CLIP embeddings generation
│   ├── test_model.py            # Model evaluation and testing
│   └── wandb_utils.py           # Wandb integration utilities
├── datasets/
│   ├── raw/                     # Raw image datasets (organized by class folders)
│   └── normalized/              # Processed datasets with embeddings
├── pipeline_cli.py              # Rich CLI interface for full pipeline
└── .cursorrules                 # This file
```

## Key Technologies & Dependencies
- **PyTorch Lightning**: Training framework with callbacks and loggers
- **OpenCLIP**: CLIP model implementations (especially SigLIP variants)
- **Wandb**: Experiment tracking with image visualization
- **Rich**: Beautiful CLI interfaces and progress displays
- **NumPy/Pandas**: Data processing
- **PIL**: Image processing
- **Windows Compatible**: All Unicode issues resolved (ASCII-only outputs)

## Core Components

### 1. MultiLayerPerceptron (train_model_mlp.py)
- PyTorch Lightning module with configurable hidden layers
- Default architecture: (4096, 1024, 512, 128) → num_classes
- Metrics: Accuracy, F1, Precision, Recall (train/val)
- Validation visualization every 5 epochs (epochs 0, 5, 10, 15...)
- SimpleDashboard for real-time training feedback
- Multiple optimizers: Lion (default), Adam, Prodigy, Lamb

### 2. Pipeline Workflow
1. **CSV Generation**: Raw images → structured CSV with labels
2. **Embedding Generation**: Images → CLIP embeddings (.npy files)
3. **Model Training**: Embeddings → trained MLP model
4. **Model Testing**: Evaluation on test set

### 3. CLI Interfaces
- **pipeline_cli.py**: Rich spinner interface, disables dashboard (--no-dashboard)
- **Direct script**: Full ASCII dashboard with real-time metrics
- **Execution methods**:
  ```bash
  # Pipeline CLI (Rich spinner)
  python pipeline_cli.py --dataset tattoo --train-only --epochs 120
  
  # Direct script (ASCII dashboard)
  python src/train_model_mlp.py -i datasets/normalized/tattoo --epochs 120
  ```

### 4. SimpleDashboard Class
- ASCII-only progress bars (#/- characters)
- Displays: epoch progress, timing, metrics table, learning rate, system stats
- Prints every validation epoch (every 5 epochs)
- Safety checks for PyTorch Lightning sanity checking
- Status indicators: DOWN/UP/WAIT, GOOD/OK/TRAIN, GREAT/GOOD/TRAIN

## CLIP Models & Configurations
**Primary Model**: `"hf-hub:timm", "ViT-SO400M-14-SigLIP-384"`
- High-quality SigLIP variant with 384px resolution
- Other supported: ViT-B/32, ViT-L/14, various SigLIP models
- Embedding dimensions automatically detected via `open_clip.get_model_config()`

## Wandb Integration
- **Project Name**: "aesthetica-training"
- **Validation Visualization**: Image predictions logged every 25 epochs OR every 5 validation runs
- **Metrics Logged**: All training/validation metrics, learning rate, model checkpoints
- **Image Tables**: Shows actual images, true/predicted labels, confidence scores
- **API Key Management**: Stored in project root, interactive setup available

## Training Configuration
- **Validation Frequency**: Every 5 epochs (check_val_every_n_epoch=5)
- **Visualization Frequency**: Epochs 0, 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, etc.
- **Early Stopping**: 50 epochs patience on val_recall
- **Default Batch Size**: 256 (training), 32 (CLI)
- **Train/Val Split**: 75/25 with stratification when possible

## File Formats & Data Structure
- **CSV Schema**: image_path, image_name, label_name, label_id, embedding_index
- **Embeddings**: .npy files with shape (n_samples, embedding_dim)
- **Model Files**: model.pth (state_dict) + model_config.json (metadata)
- **Debug Files**: validation_debug.txt (validation run tracking)

## Windows Compatibility Notes
- **Encoding**: All Unicode characters replaced with ASCII (✓→OK, █→#, etc.)
- **Emojis**: Converted to text equivalents (">> Simple dashboard enabled!")
- **Progress Bars**: Use #/- instead of █/░
- **Status Indicators**: ASCII-only symbols throughout

## Development Patterns

### Error Handling
- Graceful degradation for missing dependencies (psutil, GPUtil)
- Try/except blocks for wandb operations
- Validation setup error checking with test methods
- Windows encoding error prevention

### Code Style
- Type hints for function parameters
- Dataclasses for configuration objects
- Rich formatting for CLI outputs
- Lightning callbacks for training lifecycle

### Testing & Validation
- `test_validation_visualization_setup()` method for debugging
- Debug file logging for validation run tracking
- Validation visualization statistics parsing in CLI

## Common Operations

### Adding New Dataset
1. Place in `datasets/raw/dataset_name/` with class subfolders
2. Run: `python pipeline_cli.py --dataset dataset_name --auto`

### Training Existing Dataset
```bash
# With Rich spinner (pipeline)
python pipeline_cli.py --dataset tattoo --train-only --epochs 120

# With ASCII dashboard (direct)
python src/train_model_mlp.py -i datasets/normalized/tattoo --epochs 120
```

### Debugging Validation Visualization
- Check `validation_debug.txt` in dataset folder
- Use `net.test_validation_visualization_setup(trainer)` method
- Ensure wandb logger is properly configured

## Important Notes
- **Dashboard Conflicts**: Pipeline CLI uses --no-dashboard to avoid Rich spinner conflicts
- **Validation Timing**: Fixed to run every 5 epochs (was only epoch 0)
- **Model Checkpointing**: Monitors val_recall for best model selection
- **System Monitoring**: Optional GPU/CPU usage display if libraries available

